<title>USA: Tetra Tech wins $10 mln EPA contract.</title>
<headline>Tetra Tech wins $10 mln EPA contract.</headline>
<dateline>PASADENA, Calif. 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tetra Tech Inc Monday said the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) has contracted with it to provide engineering and scientific services under a three-year, $10 million contract.</p>
<p>Tetra Tech will provide developmental tools for watershed planning, ecological assessments and water basin restoration, and development of water discharge standards.</p>
<p>In addition, it will support state activities, technical training, water quality computer modeling, software development and public outreach.</p>
<p>Tetra Tech shares rose 1-1/8 to close at 24-1/8 on Monday.</p>
</text>
